        "problem": "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
